keywords:
  - technical analysis
  - sequential data
  - hierarchical reduction
  - pattern recognition
  - candlestick
  - market structure
abstract: >-
  Lianxian is a deterministic, layered reduction method for financial
  sequential data. Raw candlestick series are reduced through eight
  one-way layers (L1-L8), each strictly consuming the output of the
  previous layer, producing reproducible structural annotations for
  segments, turns, patterns, and counting. The method replaces ambiguous
  discretionary judgments (e.g., pullback vs. reversal) with executable
  rules, enabling same-input-same-output verification.
